## 💰 21. Day 7 — Tokenization & Cost Economics (`ticket_classifier/cost.py`)

Day 7 integrates financial modeling and token economics analysis directly into the `ticket_classifier` production package, measuring prompt tokens, completion tokens, per-request costs, model usage breakdowns, and prompt optimization savings.

### Key Production Features

1. **Token Usage Tracking**: Every request automatically logs prompt tokens, completion tokens, total tokens, and precise estimated cost.
2. **Model Pricing Tiers**: Reusable `MODEL_PRICING` dictionary mapping token rates across **GPT-4.1**, **GPT-4.1 Mini**, and **GPT-4.1 Nano**.
3. **Model Usage Breakdown**: Tracks the exact model processing each request and prints distribution statistics.
4. **Prompt Optimization Statistics**: Measures token compression savings when removing boilerplate instructions from prompts.
5. **Language Token Inflation**: Calculates subword tokenization overhead when processing non-Latin text (e.g. Hindi / Gujarati text incurs ~146% token overhead compared to English).
6. **Automated Model Recommendation**: Automatically recommends **GPT-4.1 Nano** (<300 tokens), **GPT-4.1 Mini** (300-1000 tokens), or **GPT-4.1** (>1000 tokens) based on request token payload size.

### How to Run

```bash
python report.py
```

