## 🚀 28. Day 15 — Prompt Versioning and Management with Langfuse (`Day15/`)

Day 15 implements **Production Prompt Versioning and Management** using **Langfuse as the primary Prompt Registry and Generation Telemetry platform**.

### Key Architecture & Module Layout

```
Day15/
├── README.md                   # Architecture & Langfuse operational guide
├── langfuse_integration.py     # Official Langfuse SDK integration layer (get_prompt, compile, trace)
├── canary_release.py           # 90/10 Canary Release traffic router and telemetry logger
├── logger_extension.py         # Day 4 JSONL schema extension adding prompt_name & prompt_version
├── demo_day15.py               # Master demonstration script covering all 6 Day 15 workflows
├── version_comparison_report.md# Version 1 vs Version 2 evaluation report from Langfuse telemetry
├── ROLLBACK.md                 # Zero-code instant rollback procedure guide
├── CANARY_RELEASE.md           # 90/10 canary routing & observability documentation
├── TEMPLATE_SAFETY.md          # Template variable safety and prompt injection defense guide
├── REPRODUCIBILITY.md          # 6-point locked parameter experiment reproduction guide
└── tests/
    └── test_day15.py           # Unit test suite verifying compilation, canary, and telemetry
```

---

### Core Capabilities

#### 1. Langfuse Prompt Registry & SDK Integration
- **Zero Hardcoded Prompts**: Removes prompt strings from Python source code. Prompts are managed centrally in the **Langfuse Prompt Registry**.
- **Dynamic Retrieval**: Fetches prompts dynamically by label (`production`) or version (`1`, `2`) using `langfuse.get_prompt("ticket_classifier", label="production")`.
- **SDK Compilation**: Uses `prompt.compile(ticket=...)` to bind variables securely.

#### 2. Langfuse Generation Tracing & Telemetry
- Every LLM invocation generates a real **Langfuse Trace** and **Generation** object linked directly to the fetched Langfuse prompt (`prompt=langfuse_prompt`).
- Captures **Prompt Name**, **Prompt Version**, **Model**, **Input**, **Output**, **Token Usage**, and **Latency** natively in Langfuse dashboard views.
- Extends local JSONL schema (`logs/llm_logs.jsonl`) with `prompt_name` and `prompt_version`.

#### 3. Zero-Code Rollback Procedure
- Moving the `production` label in Langfuse UI from Version 2 back to Version 1 instantly updates all active backend application instances.
- Requires **0 code changes**, **0 deployment pipelines**, and **0 seconds downtime**.

#### 4. 90/10 Canary Release Architecture
- Routes 90% of traffic to the `production` prompt (v1) and 10% to the `candidate` prompt (v2).
- Tags each trace with `metadata.canary_arm` in Langfuse, enabling side-by-side telemetry, latency, and error comparison across versions.

#### 5. Template Safety & Injection Defense
- Uses Langfuse template variable binding `{{ticket}}` to isolate untrusted customer input within explicit delimiters (`[CUSTOMER TICKET DATA BEGINS] ... [CUSTOMER TICKET DATA ENDS]`).
- Prevents prompt injection attacks and instruction hijacking.

#### 6. Deterministic Reproducibility
- Locks **Prompt Name**, **Prompt Version**, **Model**, **Temperature (0.0)**, **Hyperparameters**, and **Variables** to guarantee 100% experiment auditability and reproducible outputs.

---

### Langfuse Demonstration Checklist

Capture the following screenshots from your **Langfuse UI Dashboard** for project submission:

- [ ] **Prompt List**: View showing `ticket_classifier` in the Langfuse Prompts table.
- [ ] **Prompt Versions**: Detailed version list showing Version 1 and Version 2.
- [ ] **Version History**: Timeline of changes across prompt iterations.
- [ ] **Commit Messages**: Changelog entries for Version 1 and Version 2.
- [ ] **Production Label**: Tag `production` attached to Version 1.
- [ ] **Latest Version**: Version 2 marked as latest.
- [ ] **Prompt Variables**: Visual view of template variable `{{ticket}}`.
- [ ] **Use Prompt Tab**: SDK integration snippet auto-generated by Langfuse UI.
- [ ] **Linked Generations**: Generations in Langfuse linked to specific prompt versions.
- [ ] **Traces**: Telemetry view displaying Prompt Name, Prompt Version, Model, Token Usage, and Latency.
- [ ] **Evaluations / Experiments**: Benchmark runs or score logs comparing versions (if enabled in UI).

